			"Message": "fix(Land): Advance Element submodules — dev build isolation, module resolution, and dependency fixes\n\nAdvance all six Element submodules to their latest revisions, addressing build artifact, dependency, and module resolution issues across the editor stack.\n\nMountain renames the crate binary, library, package, Tauri productName, and bundle identifier to a verbose development build descriptor (encoding Node 22, VS Code dependency, debug profile, esbuild compiler), preventing binary name and macOS bundle ID collisions with the release build. The Tauri resource bundle expands to include all Sky deployment variant directories that were previously omitted. This enables side-by-side installation and testing of development and release builds.\n\nSky replaces three bare `@codeeditorland/sky` package specifiers in workbench layout entry points (Bundled Electron, standalone Electron, Mountain Tauri) with explicit relative paths resolving to `Function/Sky/Bridge.js`. This ensures deterministic module resolution when the build pipeline does not alias the package name to the Sky source directory, preventing resolution failures or duplicate bridge module copies.\n\nOutput adds the missing `browserslist` dependency to its package manifest, resolving an unhandled peer dependency that could cause build failures in downstream consumers.\n\nCocoon regenerates all compiled JavaScript output to pick up the latest extension-host API fidelity source changes, folding several Target files into a single consolidated bootstrap pipeline routed through `Target/Effect/RPCServer.js`.\n\nMaintain relocates the `IsFreeVarSafe` check and `FindSubstSite` resolution from the main eliminator loop in Inline.rs into `TryBlockPreserve` in mod.rs, where the Preserve-pass text-patching logic actually consumes them. Flattens multi-line function signatures, replaces wildcard destructuring with rest patterns, and reflows doc comments. Behaviour across both Preserve and AST-rebuild paths remains identical.\n\nWind regenerates its TypeScript incremental build metadata file, reflecting updated program structure and declaration maps after module resolution changes in the project.\n\nDevelopment builds now install side-by-side with release builds without bundle identifier conflicts, all workbench entry points resolve the Sky bridge deterministically, and the missing browserslist dependency is restored.",
			"SHA": "ad1d49c23687df1619a1eeb2394db0d376337a91"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-25T19:12:27Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⠇⠀⠀⠀",
				26,
				7
			],
			"Message": "feat(Land): Advance Element submodules — extension env collections, decoration rendering, tier routing expansion\n\nAdvance all seven Element submodules to their latest revisions, closing systemic gaps across the extension-host API surface, decoration pipeline, and IPC routing infrastructure.\n\nCocoon replaces a dozen no-op stubs with real implementations: EnvironmentVariableCollection mutations forward to Mountain via terminal.envCollection.* notifications; workspaceState/globalState caches prime before activate(); extensionUri uses MakeUri() for asset resolution; registerTextEditorCommand drives edits atomically through TextEditorEdit; language provider metadata (documentSelector, triggerCharacters, codeActionKinds) flows to Mountain for correct Monaco invocation; executeTask returns a real task handle; LogOutputChannel provides ISO-8601 timestamped, level-filtered output; status bar items support the 1.74+ overloads with idempotent disposal; webview panels gain live viewColumn/active/visible tracking; tree data providers subscribe onDidChangeTreeData for refresh; webviewView providers forward retainContextWhenHidden; setStatusBarMessage supports all three upstream overloads; filesystem writes encode binary as Uint8Array; applyEdit returns Mountain's actual success boolean. Also adds __LandTier_* esbuild defines for 15 subsystems with registration in RouteManifest.\n\nMountain implements TerminalEnvCollection — a global registry dispatching Replace/Append/Prepend/Delete/Clear/SetPersistent/SetDescription from seven vine terminal.envCollection.* handlers, applying registered mutators at every PTY spawn via ApplyToEnv. Adds tree.refresh and outputChannel.replace Vine notification relays. Expands tier routing defaults to 14 additional subsystems matching Cocoon's tier definitions, and extends LandFixTier::LogResolvedTiers to emit all 16 values at boot.\n\nOutput exposes ICodeEditorService on the CELExposeAccessor services facade so extension decoration APIs (createTextEditorDecorationType, setDecorationsByType) paint visible squiggles, gutter icons, and inline hints instead of silently no-oping. Regenerates compiled Configuration tree.\n\nSky registers decoration types directly with ICodeEditorService in InstallTasksAndDecorations, switches setDecorations to setDecorationsByType, wires panel-mode webview lifecycle with postMessage/dispose/viewState forwarding back to Cocoon, adds sky://output/replace handler for atomic channel replacement, and relays sky://tree-view/refresh from Cocoon to ITreeView.refresh().\n\nWind adds 14 per-subsystem IPC routing tier definitions (Terminal, SCM, Debug, LanguageFeatures, Search, OutputChannel, NativeHost, TreeView, Storage, Model, Tasks, Auth, Encryption, ExtensionHost, WebSocket) with union types and defaults matching .env.Land profiles.\n\nWorker adds deepmerge-ts 7.1.5 for type-safe recursive configuration merging in the ESBuild pipeline.\n\nRest normalises shell redirection spacing and case indentation across Bench.sh, prepublishOnly.sh, and run_tests.sh.\n\nExtension environment variables now survive reload, decorations paint on first render, webview panels remain interactive, output channels update atomically, tree views respond to data changes, and the IPC tier routing layer covers all 16 subsystems across the Mountain ↔ Cocoon ↔ Wind ↔ Sky stack.",
			"SHA": "c7f7c6da1c6a274cdbe39651bf5e8bc9fd16a6db"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
